  "description": "How deep an agent sits in the delegation tree, and how every surface draws that depth. The project service derives the depth once in build_project_topology by walking the supervision edge (`watchedBy`, the role registry's watchBindings) among the sessions of one checkout; the TUI and the Expo app each only multiply it. Before this, depth was a two-level flag -- worktree at 0 and everything inside it at 1 -- so both renderers indented with a boolean and a three-level org read as one flat list of peers. A row whose manager is not among these rows says so with `managerNotShown`, because the indent cannot: unmarked, it reads exactly like an agent nobody manages. Every case pins the row ORDER too, because an indent is only a tree if a manager is drawn above its reports.",
